#
# B-010: /healthz stops telling the whole subnet what this installation is.
#
# The previous image delivered the initial screen and recorded this exposure WITHOUT
# repairing it, on the grounds that the repair touches three platform installers and the
# update manager's health poll. It does touch them. It does not break them — and that was
# never checked before the item was deferred.
#
# What /healthz disclosed, to any host on this LAN bind, with no session at all: the exact
# product version (which names the build to look up in a vulnerability list), the authority
# posture, the PostgreSQL and pgvector server versions, the full component inventory, the
# update channel and the enabled debug scopes. It is the same class /metrics closed four
# phases ago on the neighbouring route, which is the point — the rule existed and this
# endpoint simply never asked it.
#
# What this image changes:
#
#   1. the route is SPLIT, not authenticated. Every consumer — the container healthcheck,
#      the three platform installers, Test-Noesar.ps1, verify-runtime.sh, the update
#      manager's post-start poll — reads exactly three things: `status`, `local`, and the
#      HTTP status code. All three stay open to everyone, because a 401 there reads as a
#      dead service. The status code is still computed from the FULL health, so an unhealthy
#      installation still answers 503 to a probe it will not explain itself to;
#   2. the detail moves behind the gate, and a redacted body DECLARES that it is redacted,
#      naming the role and the permission it would take. Empty-and-silent and forbidden look
#      identical on a screen, and only one of them means "there is nothing here" — the same
#      rule as UI-036 and D-0165;
#   3. the gate is owner AND audit.read, not audit.read alone. `admin` carries audit.read,
#      so a permission-only test would have handed admins exactly what the initial screen
#      and the Health section withhold from them — building the shortcut around the gate
#      while believing it was closing one. The condition now exists ONCE, in
#      auth.mjs::mayReadHealthDetail, pure and exported so it is testable without starting a
#      listener, and /api/v1/home was rewritten to use it instead of its own copy;
#   4. the exposure rule is likewise one predicate with two named views over it. The second
#      endpoint that needed it went uncovered for four phases because it did not have it at
#      all; a third one deciding for itself is how they drift.
#
# Measured, not asserted: 745 unit tests (734 + 11 new), 315 browser checks in a real
# browser (312 + 3 — the owner's Health panel is now rendered and read, because the suite
# previously only proved a RESTRICTED role is denied it, which passes just as well when the
# panel is broken for the owner too), 27/27 WCAG 2.2 AA across 729 controls, ESLint over 170
# files with no errors and no no-undef, MANIFEST 5738/5738. Both halves of the fix were seen
# to FAIL first: seeding unconditional disclosure back in fails the LAN behaviour test, and
# seeding the permission-only gate fails the admin test and only that one.
#
# ROLLBACK COST — none new (CLAUDE10.md 11d).
#
# `AI_STATE_VERSION` does NOT move: it stays at 3. Nothing here adds a collection or a field
# to a record, and no stored record changes shape — the repair is entirely in how a response
# is composed. Rolling back to :phase4-home is therefore only starting the preserved
# container, and it reinstates the disclosure. The cost declared by :phase4-parts still
# stands on its own terms — an image older than that one refuses a workspace written at
# version 3 — and that condition is unchanged by this build.
#
# Lineage, stated rather than hidden — now thirteen deep:
#
#   node:22-bookworm-slim@sha256:6c74791e…
#     -> :phase3 -> :phase4 -> :phase4-complete -> :phase4-complete-lan
#     -> :phase4-webui -> :phase4-wp2 -> :phase4-structure -> :phase4-tokens
#     -> :phase4-themes -> :phase4-parts -> :phase4-home -> :phase4-healthz -> :phase4-reasoning -> :phase4-capability
#
# Only the control plane changes. apps/webui-static is untouched by this phase and is
# deliberately NOT re-copied: copying an unchanged tree would make the image differ from its
# parent for no reason and cost a layer that proves nothing.
#
# Built with --network=none --pull=false.
FROM noesar-evolution:phase4-reasoning

USER root
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/src/ /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/src/
USER 10001:10001
